  "result": "Excellent! All 162 tests pass (143 original + 19 new payments tests). Here's what I implemented:\n\n\u2705 **Created `src/payments.js`** with two functions:\n\n1. **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`**\n   - Records a payment on an issued or partially_paid invoice\n   - Amount must be a positive integer (in cents)\n   - Date must be valid YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - Creates `invoice.payments` array if missing\n   - Appends payment to existing array (never mutates original)\n   - Sets status automatically:\n     - 'paid' when payments fully cover the invoice total\n     - 'partially_paid' while balance remains\n   - Errors:\n     - `NOT_ISSUED`: if status isn't 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n     - `AMOUNT_INVALID`: if amount isn't a positive integer\n     - `DATE_INVALID`: if date isn't in valid YYYY-MM-DD format\n     - `OVERPAYMENT`: if payment exceeds balance due\n\n2. **`balanceDue(invoice)`**\n   - Returns total amount still owed (total - sum of payments)\n   - Works with invoices that have no payments array\n   - Uses `invoiceTotals` to calculate the invoice total\n\n\u2705 **Added error codes to `src/errors.js`:**\n- `NOT_ISSUED`\n- `OVERPAYMENT`\n\n\u2705 **Comprehensive tests** (19 new) covering:\n- `balanceDue` calculations with various payment scenarios\n- `recordPayment` creating and appending payments\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- All error conditions\n- Immutability of invoice objects\n- Payment on partially_paid invoices\n- Field preservation across payment recording\n\n\u2705 **All house rules followed:**\n- No mutations (always creates new payments array)\n- Amounts always in cents\n- Tests pass",
